  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies two gate-based quantum fraud-detection experiments: a QSVM and a QGNN, both run with 4 qubits and circuit depth 3. On the IEEE-CIS dataset, QSVM reaches 96.5% accuracy and 0.95 AUC, while QGNN reaches 97.3% accuracy and 0.97 AUC; the main classical baselines range from 91.2% accuracy for logistic regression to 96.1% for a 3-layer DNN. The paper reports empirical improvements, but no asymptotic speedup or crossover analysis, so the results remain NISQ-scale demonstrations rather than proven practical quantum advantage.",
